abilities hidden by isotropic truncations, and change the moduli hierarchies relevant to small-field inflation?","connectionCount":3,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f37e264206d899f7bb4bbf7156a98c308d233afae86c196251439d7107d04cab","title":"Which gauge algebras can cancel local anomalies when ten-dimensional N=1 supergravity, containing one two-form, is coupled to adjoint N=1 super Yang–Mills?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0019"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f3324ac2bf5119569b7517296bb4fd85c3a4d91f0e8651a8444e7f15881868d5","title":"Can the Einstein–Hilbert truncation underlying Asymptotic Safety yield an intrinsically two-dimensional fixed-point theory compatible with Hilbert space positivity, and what are its central charge and gravitational dressing?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f310cc62291d0ad9f437d30c8ec3785fc47aca44dde7189d98d5912091cc6017","title":"Can a charged test particle destroy a GMGHS dilaton black hole, does a hoop-based treatment restore censorship, and does entropy increase during the proposed merger impose a weak-gravity-type charge-to-mass bound?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f3a465374d22aaf2d1e3386d43dc37f9a56b33abf3d360c38be1fb895de2fafb","title":"Does a gravitationally generated axion harmonic preserve the QCD axion's cancellation of strong CP? The reviewed model compares a QCD cosine minimized at zero with a second cosine of the same period and a generic relative phase.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0029"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:f3a8dbe37d81209f7d9f907da65f860571bd18d1537c44bbaae7067c10601b5f","title":"Could a restriction involving